{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nThe outbound comment sync re-posted duplicate comments to Jira on every hourly pass\n(bug `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker` / `aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`: the PRIMARY comment-id dedup map\n`comment_ids` is inert/empty, leaving only the lossy body-membership fallback). The\nreconcile-bridge workflow is **paused** (`disabled_manually`, confirmed via the Actions API),\nso the duplicate set is FIXED and no longer growing. **REB-1861** is pinned at Jira's\n5000-comment HARD cap, so new comments on it fail with `COMMENTS_PER_ISSUE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`.\nThis ticket purges the accumulated duplicates.\n\nSame failure class, different route, as bug `florid-vigorous-urial` (`1f3d-cb66-d3fc-4356`);\nits cleanup task `bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f` (extrovert-dippy-bongo) is the established precedent and\nits mechanism is reused here rather than reinvented.\n\n## How the affected-issue set is enumerated (deterministic, not a guess)\n\nThe set is derived from the LAST reconcile pass before the pause — GitHub Actions run\n**32403944666** of `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` (2026-08-20T18:34Z). Every issue the\nreconciler touched emits `RECON: outbound_update key=<KEY> changed=[...] comments=<N>`; the\naffected set is exactly the keys with `comments>0`, i.e. the issues for which the pass computed\npending comment adds. Reproduce with:\n\n```\ngh run view 32403944666 --log \\\n  | grep -oE \"RECON: outbound_update key=[A-Z]+-[0-9]+ changed=\\[[^]]*\\] comments=[0-9]+\" \\\n  | sed -E 's/.*key=([A-Z]+-[0-9]+).*comments=([0-9]+)/\\1 \\2/' | awk '$2>0'\n```\n\nThat yields **30 issues** (the bug ticket's \"~28\" estimate). Keys with `comments=0` in that pass\nare converged and cannot be carrying duplicates from this bug: the body-membership fallback is\ndeterministic, so an issue that matches today matched on every prior pass. The enumerated list is\nthe completeness baseline for the run, is written to an artifact, and drives the script; the\nrun is REFUSED if the key list and the artifact disagree.\n\nMeasured damage (read-only dry run over that list; all 30 passed the completeness check):\n\n| Jira key | Jira total | unmarked (never touched) | distinct bot bodies | duplicates to delete |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| REB-1861 | 5000 | 5000 | 0 | 79 | 4921 |\n| REB-1580 | 2943 | 2943 | 0 | 45 | 2898 |\n| REB-1829 | 2521 | 2521 | 0 | 37 | 2484 |\n| REB-3067 | 771 | 771 | 0 | 31 | 740 |\n| REB-2823 | 2107 | 2107 | 0 | 37 | 2070 |\n| REB-2882 | 1536 | 1536 | 0 | 24 | 1512 |\n| … | … | … | … | … |\n\n(Full 30-row table is recorded as a comment on this ticket; artifact `logs/dryrun-all.txt`.)\n\n**Totals: 31,683 Jira comments; 30,847 bot-marked; 836 unmarked; 836 distinct bodies kept;\n30,011 duplicates to delete.**\n\n## Mechanism (reused from bd80 — see that ticket for the full rationale)\n\n- **Bot identification — the safety-critical filter. Marker detection runs on the PRE-STRIP\n  rendered text.** A comment is a deletion candidate IFF\n  `adf.adf_to_text(comment[\"body\"])` — the raw ADF→text render, with NO marker strip — contains\n  `RECONCILER_MARKER = \"<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->\"` (`outbound_comments.py`, appended by\n  `_decorate_outbound_comment`). This is deliberately NOT `_normalize_comment_body`, which\n  STRIPS the marker before returning and therefore can never be used for detection. The two uses\n  are kept separate and explicit:\n  *detection* = `adf.adf_to_text(body)` (pre-strip);\n  *dedup grouping* = `_normalize_comment_body(body)` (post-strip).\n  A comment whose pre-strip rendered text lacks the marker is treated as foreign and is NEVER a\n  deletion candidate in phase 1.\n- **Secondary cross-check.** All candidates on an issue must resolve to a single bot\n  `author.accountId`; divergence aborts that issue for manual review. (Observed homogeneous:\n  `712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e` — the same accountId bd80 recorded.)\n- **Dedup key = the reconciler's OWN normalization.** Group candidates by\n  `outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body(body)`, imported and reused verbatim, so \"distinct\n  body\" means exactly what the reconciler means by it.\n- **Keep-one rule.** Per distinct normalized body: keep the OLDEST copy (min `created`), delete\n  the rest. A body with only ONE copy is NEVER deleted. This structurally guarantees the\n  invariant that every distinct body retains exactly one instance.\n- **Pagination + completeness gate.** All comments are fetched via\n  `GET /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/comment?startAt=..&maxResults=100&orderBy=created` and the count\n  is reconciled against the `total` from `?maxResults=0`. `len(fetched) != total` REFUSES that\n  issue (guards a silently truncated fetch producing a dangerous delete list).\n- **Rate limiting — 429 IS retried, explicitly.** The DELETE does NOT go through\n  `delete_comment`/`_direct_rest_delete`, which re-raise 4xx/5xx immediately and would hard-abort\n  on the first 429 across ~30k calls. Every request (GET and DELETE) goes through the script's own\n  request wrapper, which honours `Retry-After` on HTTP 429 and applies exponential backoff on 5xx\n  and transient connection faults, in addition to a per-call throttle. 404 on DELETE is treated as\n  idempotent success (makes re-runs safe).\n- **Append-only deletion log** (`logs/deletions.jsonl`: key, comment id, body hash, outcome,\n  timestamp) is flushed per deletion, so a mid-run stall is resumable — the keep-one grouping is\n  recomputed from the live set on every run.\n\n### Phase 2 — the 836 truncation-suffix comments (separate, evidence-gated)\n\nThree issues (REB-1567: 418, REB-1931: 278, REB-2605: 140) carry comments with NO marker. They are\nnot human: each is authored by the same bot accountId, is repeated ~139 times identically, and its\nrendered text ends with `_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX = \" … [truncated by reconciler]\"`\n(`adapters/jira/comment_limits.py`) — the reconciler's own outbound truncation, which cut the\n32767-char body short and removed the trailing marker paragraph. Because the marker (the phase-1\nauthoritative identifier) is absent, these are handled as a SEPARATE phase behind an explicit\n`--include-truncated` flag, with its own dry run, under a candidate rule of: rendered text ends\nwith `_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX` AND `author.accountId` equals the resolved bot accountId. The same\nkeep-one rule applies, so the one-surviving-copy invariant is unchanged. Phase 2 is not required\nto clear the cap and can be declined without affecting phase 1.\n\n## Safety plan (T4 — irreversible)\n\n- [ ] **Pre-deletion backup** of the FULL comment payload (id, ADF body, author accountId +\n      display name, created) per issue, written and completeness-checked BEFORE any DELETE.\n- [ ] **Dry-run default.** Deletion requires an explicit `--execute`. The dry run prints, per\n      issue: fetched/reported total, marked count, unmarked count, distinct-body count, the kept\n      id per body, and the delete count, and writes a per-issue machine-readable plan artifact.\n- [ ] **Canary first.** Execute on ONE light issue, verify it fully, then proceed.\n      **REB-1861 runs LAST** (largest and riskiest).\n- [ ] **Per-issue post-verification**: re-fetch and assert every distinct normalized body present\n      before the run still has exactly one surviving copy, that the unmarked count is unchanged,\n      and that the issue is below the cap.\n- [ ] Ambiguous cases are SKIPPED and reported, never guessed.\n- [ ] The reconcile-bridge workflow stays PAUSED for the whole operation and is NOT re-enabled\n      by this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The affected-issue list is derived by the documented command from run 32403944666, written\n      as an artifact, and the executed run covers exactly that list (30 issues). Proving command:\n      the enumeration command above; the script's per-issue summary lists the same keys.\n- [ ] Per issue, `len(fetched) == total` from `?maxResults=0` holds and a backup artifact exists\n      BEFORE any DELETE; a mismatch refuses that issue with no DELETE issued.\n- [ ] Dry-run output is produced and inspected before `--execute`.\n- [ ] Marker detection is on the PRE-STRIP rendered text (`adf.adf_to_text`), and the post-strip\n      `_normalize_comment_body` is used only for dedup grouping. Proving command: the dry run\n      reports non-zero `marked` counts — a detection-on-stripped-text implementation reports 0.\n- [ ] Every DELETE routes through a wrapper that honours `Retry-After` on HTTP 429 and retries\n      5xx/transient faults; a 429 does not abort the run.\n- [ ] After the run every issue is below the 5000 cap, and REB-1861 drops from 5000 to its\n      distinct-body count.\n- [ ] For every issue touched, a post-deletion re-fetch confirms zero missing distinct bodies and\n      an unchanged unmarked count (zero content loss, no human comment deleted).\n- [ ] A deletion log with one JSON object per deletion exists for the executed run; its line count\n      matches the reported delete count."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787254321974698001,"uuid":"a19f04a4-b9a8-45c6-87ba-54c0640e9f7c"}